  "note": "灵心观 inside its 山门: the square of white quartz with its lions, dragon pillars and great censer (square.c); the main hall with its red door and the round arches east and west (temple1.c, corridor1/2.c); the covered walkways of vermilion columns round the courtyard of flowers and trees with its well (inneryard.c, corridor5-7.c); the closed red door of the rear hall, the training hall, the guest rooms, the locked room west; the path of blue stones under the pines, moss creeping onto them (road1.c), round to the two-storey 藏经楼 under its blue glazed board, every door and window shut, and its tablet (road2.c). Old: the walls stained, moss in the joints, the paving worn where the feet go.",
